  "live_records": {
    "q-143859": {
      "dom_id": "step-q143859",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "The joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ for the discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ is given in the table below. Find $\\text{E}[2X+\\sqrt[3]{Y}].$\n\n| $f$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=8$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=1$ | $0.1$ | $0.2$ |\n| $X=2$ | $0.6$ | $0.1$ |",
      "worked_solution": "Suppose $X$ and $Y$ are discrete random variables with supports ${S}_{X}$ and ${S}_{Y},$ respectively, and $f(x,y)$ is their joint probability mass function with support $S={S}_{X}\\times {S}_{Y}.$ If $r:{R}^{2}\\to R$ is a function of two variables, then the rule of the lazy statistician states that\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[r(X,Y)]={\\sum }_{(x,y)\\in S}r(x,y)\\,f(x,y).\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\nr(x,y)=2x+\\sqrt[3]{y}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[2X+\\sqrt[3]{Y}] & ={\\sum }_{(x,y)\\in S}r(x,y)\\,f(x,y) \\\\  & =(2\\cdot 1+\\sqrt[3]{1})\\cdot f(1,1)+(2\\cdot 1+\\sqrt[3]{8})\\cdot f(1,8) \\\\  & \\,+(2\\cdot 2+\\sqrt[3]{1})\\cdot f(2,1)+(2\\cdot 2+\\sqrt[3]{8})\\cdot f(2,8) \\\\  & =3\\cdot f(1,1)+4\\cdot f(1,8) \\\\  & \\,+5\\cdot f(2,1)+6\\cdot f(2,8) \\\\  & =3\\cdot 0.1+4\\cdot 0.2+5\\cdot 0.6+6\\cdot 0.1 \\\\  & =0.3+0.8+3+0.6 \\\\  & =4.7.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
